WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.130 --> 00:00:05.046
(bouncy, energetic Christmas music)

00:00:06.283 --> 00:00:11.172
(bouncy, happy jazz music)

00:00:13.532 --> 00:00:14.888
- Hi, I'm Hannah,

00:00:14.888 --> 00:00:17.142
and I'm addicted to Christmas sweaters.

00:00:17.142 --> 00:00:20.473
My sweater collection started
probably six years ago.

00:00:20.473 --> 00:00:24.415
I bought a sweater vest on
eBay and it smelled horrible,

00:00:24.415 --> 00:00:26.450
but it was just the
funniest thing in the world,

00:00:26.450 --> 00:00:29.994
and it snowballed into
this long-running joke

00:00:29.994 --> 00:00:33.603
of just buying any
vintage Christmas sweater

00:00:33.603 --> 00:00:34.741
I could get my hands on.

00:00:34.741 --> 00:00:37.224
My mom joined in, and
together we have a collection

00:00:37.224 --> 00:00:40.395
of upwards of 350.

00:00:40.395 --> 00:00:41.289
I know I'm crazy.

00:00:41.289 --> 00:00:43.485
I'll be the first one to
say, "I'm totally insane."

00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:44.680
This is a good crazy.

00:00:44.680 --> 00:00:46.085
It's fun.

00:00:46.085 --> 00:00:48.892
I wear one every day of
the month of December.

00:00:48.892 --> 00:00:50.243
And it makes people happy.

00:00:50.243 --> 00:00:52.157
I walk down the street
and people are like,

00:00:52.157 --> 00:00:53.340
"That's a cool sweater."

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.439
The sweaters are so cool.

00:00:54.439 --> 00:00:56.956
If you just spent the time
to just look through each one

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:59.726
and see how funny and cool they are.

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.365
I think it's awesome.

00:01:02.256 --> 00:01:04.502
My idol, the only person I'd like to meet

00:01:04.502 --> 00:01:06.486
if I could meet anyone in the world,

00:01:06.486 --> 00:01:08.216
it would be Michael Simon.

00:01:08.216 --> 00:01:10.279
He does the most brilliant designs,

00:01:10.279 --> 00:01:13.482
the most in your face,
disgusting Christmas barf

00:01:13.482 --> 00:01:14.607
all over everything.

00:01:14.607 --> 00:01:16.812
Wherever you go in a
Michael Simon sweater,

00:01:16.812 --> 00:01:18.972
like people know that you're there

00:01:18.972 --> 00:01:21.333
because they can sense the Christmas

00:01:21.333 --> 00:01:22.703
coming off your sweater.

00:01:22.703 --> 00:01:25.710
If I had to guess how
much money we've spent

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.358
on Christmas sweaters,
it's probably about $2,000.

00:01:28.358 --> 00:01:32.360
We have a few sweaters that
are going for about $500 now.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.194
The character ones are insanely popular,

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:38.291
so I think we could probably
triple what we spent

00:01:38.291 --> 00:01:40.030
if we sold all of them.

00:01:40.030 --> 00:01:41.887
But now we're kind of attached,

00:01:41.887 --> 00:01:44.367
so I think we're gonna keep 'em all.

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:47.908
It's impossible to make
an ugly Christmas sweater.

00:01:47.908 --> 00:01:49.171
Like the way you'd make it is,

00:01:49.171 --> 00:01:52.736
"How do I make a really
nice Christmas sweater?"

00:01:52.736 --> 00:01:53.984
And that's what these are.

00:01:53.984 --> 00:01:56.558
When you see the ones now
that are trying to be ugly,

00:01:56.558 --> 00:01:57.565
you can tell the difference.

00:01:57.565 --> 00:01:58.506
It's not authentic.

00:01:58.506 --> 00:02:01.234
It's not an actual Christmas sweater

00:02:01.234 --> 00:02:04.251
with the intent of
looking really glamorous.

00:02:04.251 --> 00:02:07.083
I like that this is a thing
that's brought my mom and I

00:02:07.083 --> 00:02:08.069
really close.

00:02:08.069 --> 00:02:10.449
Literally the only reason we
have it is because it makes

00:02:10.449 --> 00:02:11.736
people happy.

00:02:11.736 --> 00:02:15.739
So, that's probably my favorite
part about owning all these.

00:02:16.602 --> 00:02:19.016
The mailman really, really
hated my mom for a while,

00:02:19.016 --> 00:02:22.720
because he'd come with just
this giant bin full of packages

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:25.600
'cause we'd have like 15
sweaters coming at a time

00:02:25.600 --> 00:02:26.581
on the reg.

00:02:26.581 --> 00:02:27.467
(laughter)

00:02:28.447 --> 00:02:29.251
(creaking)

